"Places multiple quantitative axes around a center and connects each record’s values into a profile polygon.\n\nUse when: A few comparable normalized metrics need a familiar profile overview. Only one or a small number of records must be compared.\n\nAvoid when: Exact value comparison, unrelated scales, or numerous overlapping profiles are required.\n\nVisual grammar: Radial distance on each spoke encodes one metric on a declared scale. The connected polygon identifies one record, while spoke angle is a layout choice.\n\nBuild: Choose a fixed metric order and consistent direction of better performance. Normalize only with documented meaningful bounds and show radial ticks. Plot one or very few profiles with short spoke labels beyond the polygons.\n\nCheck: Check every spoke’s scale and zero interpretation are explicit. Verify metric order stays identical across comparison panels. Confirm values outside the chosen bounds are not silently clipped.\n\nPitfalls: Polygon area changes when spoke order changes and is not a valid overall score. Overlapping edges and crossings may be intrinsic; prefer a dot plot or heatmap for precise comparisons.\n\nExample: Compare synthetic product profiles across five normalized quality metrics, with explicit bounds and a fixed spoke order.\n\nAlternatives: Parallel coordinates, Heatmap, Dot plot."
